# Polling vs MQTT Push

## HTTP Polling
- ESP32 calls GET /telemetry/latest every 30-60 seconds
- Simple to implement
- Higher latency (up to 60s delay)
- Uses more battery (wake, connect, request, sleep)
- Good for: dashboards, non-critical reads

## MQTT Push
- Broker pushes data instantly when available
- Lower latency (milliseconds)
- More efficient for battery
- Good for: irrigation commands, alerts, real-time control

## When to prefer MQTT over HTTP Poll
- When you need instant command delivery
- When battery life matters
- When data changes faster than polling interval
- For irrigation trigger commands (Day 13+)